          "explanation": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><p>Standard error: $\\sigma_{\\bar{X}} = \\dfrac{10}{\\sqrt{16}} = 2.5$. Standardize: $z_{1} = \\dfrac{45-45}{2.5} = 0$ and $z_{2} = \\dfrac{52-45}{2.5} = 2.8$. So $P(45 < \\bar{X} < 52) = P(Z < 2.8) - P(Z < 0) = 0.9974 - 0.5 = 0.4974$. (Using $\\sigma = 10$ instead of the standard error would give $z_2 = 0.7$ — a common error.)</p></div><div class=\"ml-vi\"><p>Sai số chuẩn: $\\sigma_{\\bar{X}} = \\dfrac{10}{\\sqrt{16}} = 2{,}5$. Chuẩn hoá: $z_{1} = \\dfrac{45-45}{2{,}5} = 0$ và $z_{2} = \\dfrac{52-45}{2{,}5} = 2{,}8$. Vậy $P(45 < \\bar{X} < 52) = P(Z < 2{,}8) - P(Z < 0) = 0{,}9974 - 0{,}5 = 0{,}4974$. (Dùng nhầm $\\sigma = 10$ thay vì sai số chuẩn sẽ ra $z_2 = 0{,}7$ — lỗi rất hay gặp.)</p></div>"
